.SH AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
An auth on action policy can ask for a login again before these actions.
See
.B Auth On Action Policy
in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
A unit has the hooks every object type has, and these; a command of another name is in brackets:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
set_config_parameter\ (config).
.hy
.ad
.RE
.PP
It also has
.B pre_add_<type>
before an object of that type is added below the unit, and
.B post_add_<type>
after it, e.g.
.BR pre_add_user .
\fI<type>\fR is one of:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
accessgroup, aclgroup, ca, client, device, dictionary, group, host, node, pass, policy, pool, resolver, role, scope, script, share, unit, user, vlan.
.hy
.ad
.RE
.\" END AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm, on the nodes and, by sync, on the hosts.
A unit is the directory \fI<unit>.unit\fR in the directory of its site, or of the unit above it, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/linux.unit/users.unit/\fR, with its settings in \fIobject.json\fR.
The objects of the unit are in it as \fI<name>.<type>\fR.
Change them with the commands above, not in the files.
.hy
.ad
